<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ab65a308-4f6e-587e-b366-89b82649a167" activityNameId="37e92c31-aed2-5a2e-bb0f-b45d1df1c4dd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Building, multi-storey</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Building, multi-storey
The combination of two concrete buildings, one built in 1927 and the other in 1972, makes this module a sort of average of existing multi-storey buildings. The life of the building is assumed to be 80 years. This module should not be used if its relative importance would be high in a certain environmental inventory.;
Synonyms: multi-story, house, Haus; 
UUID: 552ee3f6-4f6a-3b85-a72c-5707a3b0f9c7
Includes the most important materials used and their disposal, the transportation of the parts to the building site and to the final disposal at the end of life. Also included is the requirement of electricity for construction, maintenance and demolition. Operation is not included.
Location: Certain elementary flows or intermediate product flows are RER, UCPTE or GLO modules
Technology: The two concrete multi-storey buildings used to make this module were built in 1927 and 1972, but they can be assumed to reflect a sort of average of existing buildings as they are weighted.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: most data obtained by personal communication 
Extrapolations: See geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_552ee3f6-4f6a-3b85-a72c-5707a3b0f9c7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
